Served requests forward: a request carries the call pair its caller's recipe holds as two
more descriptors beside the mail pipe, and the served child adopts them as an inherited
pair, so it holds no store and sends every store call up them as a sub-make does; a run
has one store however many requests it makes. A client with no pair, a shell of its own,
serves as an owner from the store the parse left. A client whose pair its make has
dropped, a backgrounded request whose recipe ended, gets status 2 and an error line on
every store call, never a store of its own: the upward write runs with SIGPIPE ignored.

